# AutoAssess — project context

AutoAssess is a mobile-first damage assessment app for South African panel beaters.
The primary user is an assessor at a panel beating workshop. Workflow:
1. Scan SA vehicle licence disc (PDF417 barcode) → auto-fill vehicle details
2. Capture damage photos
3. AI analyses photos → structured damage report
4. Assessor reviews / edits
5. Generate branded PDF quote
6. Send to customer via WhatsApp / email
7. Voice-driven revisions during dismantle (versioned quotes)

## Tech stack — non-negotiable

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ App Router (no Pages Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript strict mode, no `any` unless absolutely justified
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only (no styled-components, no CSS-in-JS, no separate .module.css)
- **DB / auth / storage:** Supabase (Postgres + RLS + Storage + Auth)
- **AI:** Anthropic Claude Sonnet 4 Vision via `@anthropic-ai/sdk`
- **Barcode:** `@zxing/library` for PDF417
- **Validation:** Zod schemas for every API boundary
- **Deploy:** Vercel (web), Render (heavy background jobs)
- **Icons:** Inline SVG components in `components/ui/Icons.tsx`. Do NOT add `lucide-react` icons unless asked — keep the icon set lean.

