## Code quality — production standard

This codebase must withstand thousands of concurrent users. Reject all shortcuts:

- **No silent failures.** Every async call has try/catch with meaningful error messages.
- **No truncation for cost.** Pass full content to AI. Never reduce fidelity to save money.
- **No `any`.** Use proper types or unknown + narrow.
- **No premature optimisation, but no obvious anti-patterns.**
- **Mobile-first.** Default styles target 390px viewport, scale up with `sm:` / `md:`.
- **Accessibility.** Buttons need `aria-label` when icon-only. Images need `alt`. Form fields need `<label>`.
- **No emoji in code.** Use named SVG icons instead.

## File & folder conventions

```
app/                    # Next.js App Router pages
  page.tsx              # Home
  layout.tsx            # Root layout
  globals.css           # Tailwind directives + tokens
  api/                  # API route handlers
  [resource]/           # Resource pages (assessments, vehicles, etc.)
    page.tsx
    [id]/page.tsx
components/             # Reusable React components
  ui/                   # Shared atomic components (Icons, Button, Input)
  [Feature].tsx         # Feature-level components
lib/                    # Pure utility modules
  supabase/             # Supabase clients (server.ts, client.ts)
  schemas/              # Zod schemas
  prompts/              # AI prompt templates
  [domain].ts           # Domain helpers (disc, pricing, etc.)
```

- **Server components by default.** Add `'use client'` only when needed (state, refs, browser APIs).
- **Client components** end in client-only behaviour — wrap with `<Suspense>` in their parent when using `useSearchParams`.
- **Co-locate types** with their usage. Shared types go in `lib/types.ts`.

## South African context

- Currency: **ZAR** (R). Format: `R20,777` (comma thousands, no decimal for whole rands).
- VAT: **15%**.
- Date format: prefer `2026-05-18` (ISO) for storage, `18 May 2026` for display.
- Vehicle terminology: **bonnet** (not hood), **boot** (not trunk), **mudguard** (not fender), **windscreen** (not windshield), **number plate** (not licence plate).
- POPIA compliance: ID numbers stored as SHA-256 hashes only. Personal info access logged.
- Multi-language support planned: English, Afrikaans, Zulu, Xhosa.

## When generating code

- Match the existing design language (dark + gold, rounded-2xl/3xl, generous padding).
- Use `haptic-tap` utility class on tappable elements.
- Use `animate-fade-in` and `animate-slide-up` for entrance animations.
- Wrap mobile screens in `<main className="min-h-screen max-w-md mx-auto pb-32 safe-top safe-bottom">` pattern.
- Bottom action bars use the fixed-position gradient pattern (see existing components).
